{{--
  NOT pre-rendered, on purpose.

  Enumerating this route produced one page per judge — 2,740 of them — and with
  six such per-judge routes the SSG was emitting 20,028 pages and dying with
  "Out of memory" partway through, which also meant no sitemap.xml, no SEO head
  injection and no CSP for anything.

  Only the canonical /judges/:id page is pre-rendered now. This route is a tab
  of that page whose content is fetched client-side from the API, so a crawler
  was getting a shell plus head tags, not content — the cheapest 10,960 pages
  to give up. `preview.ts` SHELL_REWRITES serves it from the judge's own
  pre-rendered page, and the host must do the same (see DEPLOY.md).
--}}

@extends('layouts/default')

@section('title', 'Recent rulings - Bench Review')

@section('content')
  @include('Bench/Judge/ProfileHeader')
  @include('Bench/Judge/JudgeTabs')
  <div class="mx-auto px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-7xl">
    @include('Bench/Judge/RecentRulings')
  </div>
@endsection
